INSERT INTO "google_reviews" ("id","google_review_id","reviewer_name","reviewer_photo_url","star_rating","comment_text","review_created_at","review_updated_at","reply_text","reply_sent_at","reply_source","matched_client_id","match_confidence","entry_source","synced_at","created_at") VALUES('dc0627cf-4640-4732-8798-b20d292bc894','AbFvOqmwPOiPdTshb8MmEpiaV5vHe7UoVGo5AfOcvSKtV6gWkdVcw3hq9rDORvxirht2pvA4GRpb','Brooke','https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKszNFSnqHjkECzzp8Te_3EZ2Un4kpCjQ_FtASgN8FKDHoQKQ=s120-c-rp-mo-br100',5,replace('Columbus Home Solutions did a great job updating my house preparing for rental.  I moved out of state and CHS handled everything smoothly from start to finish for me. They refinished my wood floors, updated paint and installed new trim.\n\nI’d definitely recommend Columbus Home Solutions for any home improvement projects. Their attention to detail, ease of communication and quality of work is unmatched.','\n',char(10)),'2025-11-05T00:03:56.146876Z','2025-11-05T00:03:56.146876Z','Thank you so much for the kind words! We’re thrilled we could make the process smooth while you were out of state—refinishing the wood floors, refreshing the paint, and installing new trim were great choices to get the home rental-ready. Our team takes pride in clear communication, attention to detail, and quality craftsmanship, so your feedback means a lot. If you ever need help with future turnovers or maintenance in Central Arkansas, we’re here for you. —Tony & the Columbus Home Solutions team','2025-11-12T18:10:39.275300Z','external',NULL,NULL,'sync','2026-08-23 21:30:28','2026-07-20 02:06:45');
INSERT INTO "google_reviews" ("id","google_review_id","reviewer_name","reviewer_photo_url","star_rating","comment_text","review_created_at","review_updated_at","reply_text","reply_sent_at","reply_source","matched_client_id","match_confidence","entry_source","synced_at","created_at") VALUES('d23c38a9-3248-4cbb-9174-e665491deb00','AbFvOqlzwIDCCqXKkQkZNNHufRlhRmIK2PTGxjG1fdu3fvh1Qn-SGthpEcS0U5XHBkqsKXabyKW77w','Aaron Winward','https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVPFMn1WKgdJBGkB8XxlYTr6LLzgjv7rdGQ4IA_Y-qVZbuLP83rtw=s120-c-rp-mo-br100',5,'We had a great experience with Tony at Columbus Home Solutions! He came highly recommended and we couldn’t be happier with the work! Not only did he take time out of his busy schedule to come by and check the damage with very little notice but he also stayed in constant contact throughout the process about each step of the repairs. He knocked out the job in one day and even had to build the main part from scratch because it could not be ordered. The repair to our doors look amazing and he left them in better shape than they were before the damage occurred. We highly recommend Tony at Columbus Home Solutions! 10 out of 10 on craftsmanship, customer service, and very reasonably priced for the work he did!','2025-11-04T01:18:36.865871Z','2025-11-04T01:18:36.865871Z','Thank you so much for the awesome review! I’m glad we could swing by on short notice, keep you updated through each step, and custom-build the main part so the repair could be finished in a day. Hearing that the doors look better than before—and that our craftsmanship, communication, and pricing were 10/10—means the world to us. If you need anything else, from door and trim repairs to larger projects here in Central Arkansas, we’ve got you covered.','2025-11-12T18:11:40.339197Z','external',NULL,NULL,'sync','2026-08-23 21:30:28','2026-07-20 02:06:45');
INSERT INTO "google_reviews" ("id","google_review_id","reviewer_name","reviewer_photo_url","star_rating","comment_text","review_created_at","review_updated_at","reply_text","reply_sent_at","reply_source","matched_client_id","match_confidence","entry_source","synced_at","created_at") VALUES('abaa3313-29e2-4698-bece-25293d3382bf','AbFvOqlwKDIomHoxCopXJ8hxyQDWfznnhXF7g55Db1Yusdgb1IVIw_rUxh5Mivu1hsfNJxaqgef2Uw','Cinthy Howard','https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKJVyvQT4M5qMKcGUjskTh0xOgGN0gD1V2GoFeRIulaFYGHbQ=s120-c-rp-mo-br100',5,'Tony Columbus and his crew built us an almost 650 square foot patio and an oversized 2 car garage to match our existing home.  Both of them turned out absolutely beautiful.  I cannot say enough great things about Tony and his crew.  What a wonderful bunch of guys.  They were so thoughtful and accommodating throughout the entire process and never considered any of our requests to be an inconvenience.  They showed up on time everyday and worked consistently throughout the day.  Both structures are wired for electricity and contain multiple ceiling fans.  The architecture matches well to our existing home and you would never guess that they were recent additions, as they blend seamlessly.  We have done many renovations over the last 45 years to multiple homes and I can honestly say that we have never had a better experience.  On a rating scale of 1-10, a 10 is not high enough.  I would definitely use Columbus Homes Solutions again and I highly recommend them!  You can trust Tony and his team to take great care of you.','2025-10-18T16:17:23.731771Z','2025-10-18T16:17:23.731771Z','Thank you so much for your incredible review! It was truly a pleasure working with you on your patio and oversized garage project. We’re thrilled to hear that the finished spaces blend seamlessly with your home and that you enjoyed the entire process from start to finish. Our crew takes great pride in being dependable, accommodating, and detail-oriented, so your kind words mean a lot. We’re grateful for your trust and look forward to helping you with any future projects!','2025-10-21T22:15:41.034289Z','external',NULL,NULL,'sync','2026-08-23 21:30:28','2026-07-20 02:06:45');
INSERT INTO "google_reviews" ("id","google_review_id","reviewer_name","reviewer_photo_url","star_rating","comment_text","review_created_at","review_updated_at","reply_text","reply_sent_at","reply_source","matched_client_id","match_confidence","entry_source","synced_at","created_at") VALUES('98b847c4-5eb9-4ce5-a5ec-53e4024d81b3','AbFvOqmPXvS5Fn16XCg8ifxvWEhqnHQgbfki8ZXFG0SQLaMNrF4FOnrm7ZDUruthhfU0G2TwzwJc','Shelly H','https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVro6Qe5zJzK7Wwxkpr3g-uc_eCltnznyGQB7Jdiqc1IqZShXg=s120-c-rp-mo-br100',5,'Columbus Home Solutions did amazing work on the remodel of our bathroom! They communicated, and let us know every step of what they were doing. Fair pricing and never rushed the job. Highly recommend them!','2025-10-07T22:55:29.159092Z','2025-10-07T22:55:29.159092Z','Thank you so much for your kind words! We’re thrilled to hear you’re happy with your bathroom remodel. Our team takes pride in clear communication and quality craftsmanship. We truly appreciate your trust in Columbus Home Solutions!','2025-10-10T21:36:21.183408Z','external',NULL,NULL,'sync','2026-08-23 21:30:29','2026-07-20 02:06:45');
INSERT INTO "google_reviews" ("id","google_review_id","reviewer_name","reviewer_photo_url","star_rating","comment_text","review_created_at","review_updated_at","reply_text","reply_sent_at","reply_source","matched_client_id","match_confidence","entry_source","synced_at","created_at") VALUES('9089fcf7-ba3d-4aac-819c-b2674223b917','AbFvOqkjWU5KdFZHmnemUV1CuNcu2anhTNBe7HeaOsl_4vaDlyU9QoIv8TEkPfiEzaAi51-HwhMHrA','Real Estate Christi','https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXPHpGvYn86cWh3AaG1MskRVQ6V_P3NZxT_y4xWirNXy4e_Ace2=s120-c-rp-mo-ba12-br100',5,'Seven years. SEVEN YEARS I spent rolling through general contractors for my real estate business and parting ways with each one as they botched jobs, gouged clients and communicated poorly. So when I found Tony at Columbus Home Solutions, I expected the same. I''m glad to say that I was soooo wrong. He and his crew have consistently provided wonderful craftsmanship and leave my clients happy. From building porches and decks, adding on a big garage, painting, tiling, fence work, installing floors, adding piers, framing work... it''s all been done at a fair price, good pace and top notch quality. He''s licensed, bonded and insured and will gladly provide his docs to you. I cannot reiterate how much stress it has relieved knowing that he''s a one-stop shop for me and my clients. If you have a job to bid, give him serious consideration. Highly recommend!!!!!','2025-10-07T21:10:13.861636Z','2025-10-07T21:10:13.861636Z','Thank you so much for your kind words and for trusting us with your projects!  We know how important reliability and quality are, especially in real estate, and we’re grateful for the opportunity to take that stress off your plate. Our team takes pride in delivering fair pricing, strong communication, and quality craftsmanship, and it means a lot to hear that reflected in your experience. We truly appreciate your recommendation and look forward to continuing to be your one-stop shop for future projects.','2025-10-07T22:23:16.941765Z','external',NULL,NULL,'sync','2026-08-23 21:30:29','2026-07-20 02:06:46');
INSERT INTO "google_reviews" ("id","google_review_id","reviewer_name","reviewer_photo_url","star_rating","comment_text","review_created_at","review_updated_at","reply_text","reply_sent_at","reply_source","matched_client_id","match_confidence","entry_source","synced_at","created_at") VALUES('02f6cf7d-ed1e-4e7d-92c5-b738ec0ef861','AbFvOqknN7rJYyBfK28F7ugMqznSTM6cu3GNxmqOv9vxwuWOLYErOjzOT5z-Zlily1MJ_vQ3hkiy5A','Kathleen Paul','https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKFLpAzh-xENez0cYbEo3sAWEF4JWFShqn1Sxdip6rPNtGyuQ=s120-c-rp-mo-br100',1,replace('We hired Columbus Home Solutions LLC to complete an enclosed-porch remodel, and while we are pleased with the initial work, the follow-up has been unacceptable. For more than six months, we''ve been waiting for them to return and finish loose ends they promised to address - small things that should have been wrapped up months ago.\n\nDespite mutliple calls, texts, and emails, communication has been sporadic at best and promises to "come next week" have gone unfulfilled time after time. At this point, it''s clear that reliability and professionalism are not priorities for this company. I would strongly caution anyone considering hiring Columbus Home Solutions.','\n',char(10)),'2025-10-07T02:01:11.993933Z','2025-10-07T02:01:11.993933Z','We truly appreciate your feedback and are glad you were happy with the main scope of your enclosed-porch remodel. We regret the delay in completing the small final details and understand the frustration this caused. While only one scheduled appointment was missed, we recognize that rescheduling and waiting created a poor experience, and for that we sincerely apologize. Our company has grown faster than expected, which has stretched our scheduling at times, but we are actively improving communication and follow-up to prevent this in the future. Please don’t hesitate to reach out directly so we can work with you to resolve the remaining items and restore your confidence in us.','2025-10-07T19:07:23.488822Z','external','Z2lkOi8vSm9iYmVyL0NsaWVudC84NDE1MTg5NQ==','suggested','sync','2026-08-23 21:30:29','2026-07-20 02:06:46');
INSERT INTO "google_reviews" ("id","google_review_id","reviewer_name","reviewer_photo_url","star_rating","comment_text","review_created_at","review_updated_at","reply_text","reply_sent_at","reply_source","matched_client_id","match_confidence","entry_source","synced_at","created_at") VALUES('00471797-81e1-4808-af97-237b24b5f7d2','AbFvOqmW7Jrhi-Jm6mUUG4Nto0JWq6W4RTdFXyRo7nQRRWmtWRnnypvsFlU5IM3S4ymj8k0Ps3pK','Matt Trice','https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIGOK7kQ0sjB3OsmZI_yjzPBnw-APxqD89XckloSd0V9osS=s120-c-rp-mo-ba12-br100',1,replace('The demo was done but we needed it picked up from there and finished. It took longer than anticipated, but Tony was accommodating to what we wanted and when we asked for other small things to be done during the rebuild he was gracious and did them. Overall, we are pleased with the final product.\n\nEdit 9/8/25: I''m going to have to change the review from 4 stars to 2. A little over a week ago or a month out from when the floor tile was installed we noticed the grout coming loose from the tile edges and I could feel the tile flexing under my feet. I''m not an expert but I wonder if enough thinset and/or the right trowel blade was used and if the tiles were back buttered before being placed as there seems to be hollow spaces underneath. I also noticed in many places that pieces of the tile spacers that didn''t break off right were left and grouted around.\n\nEdit 10/6/25: Changing the review to a 1 star. We''ve since had a professional flooring and tiling company come out and multiple plumbers.\n\n1. The tiles on the floor all came up in once piece. The wrong thinset was used and it was applied directly to the subfloor instead of over cement board. The wrong sized trowel was used and the thinset was troweled in different directions.\n\n2. After the tiles were removed surrounding the toilet there was standing water on top of the subfloor around the toilet. There was leaking around the toilet drain as well as leaking from the toilet supply line that was partially hidden due to the design of the bidet toilet that wasn''t discovered until toilet was being removed. There was also mold growing on the bottom of the drywall directly behind the toilet and behind the baseboard.\n\n3. Work on the shower began due to missing grout, uneven tile and shower window not being properly waterproofed. Kerdi board was used for the waterproofing which according to the company working on the shower probably kept the damage from being worse. The same issues from the floor appeared again. Wrong thinset used, wrong trowel size, and troweled thinset applied in different directions resulted in the tiles not properly adhering to the wall and the majority of the tiles were taken off in one piece with portions of the kerdi board being completely clean. I was told the grout was what probably kept the tiles from falling off the wall. Once the kerdi board was removed it was discovered that water was getting behind the wall from through the window and the insulation was soaked. The damage was caught in time and mold had not began to grow. The mixer valve was installed about 1/4" too far back as well as the pex not being installed correctly leading to leaking from the pex connections.\n\n4. Work will begin soon on opening up the wall to check for possible leaking behind the bathroom vanity and the toilet supply line. The sink drain installed is too small and hooked up in a way that results in very slow drainage. I requested for the old cast iron drain pipe to be removed and for new drain to be moved over allowing for more space and it was included in the work agreement that it would be done "move sink drain to accomodate new vanity up against wall". The cast iron pipe was left in place and instead the brand-new vanity was cut into to allow for him to run the sink plumbing while also moving the vanity over but not the sink drain as was requested.\n\nI''m paying to have the bathroom tore up again and redone correctly. Plumbers are having to tear open the wall in an adjacent room to correct the plumbing issues with the sink, toilet and shower. I''m already more out of pocket now than I was paying Columbus to do the work. I did contact Columbus, and he filed a claim with his insurance so I''m dealing with them now and will hopefully be reimbursed. I really don''t like leaving bad reviews of this nature and I know this can have an effect on his business going forward. I started to not leave anything, but this has honestly been such a nightmare, and I don''t want anyone else to have to go through this.','\n',char(10)),'2025-08-26T22:30:06.112927Z','2025-10-06T16:41:34.037192Z','Hey Matt,  I am sorry to hear about the issues that you are having and I wish you would have reached out to us regarding these issues so that we could make it right.  You have a 1 year workmanship warranty for things like this and we take our customers satisfaction very seriously.  Give me a call or shoot me a message so that we can correct this and make it right for you!','2025-09-10T17:04:25.124441Z','external','Z2lkOi8vSm9iYmVyL0NsaWVudC8xMTA5NjM1MjQ=','suggested','sync','2026-08-23 21:30:29','2026-07-20 02:06:46');
INSERT INTO "google_reviews" ("id","google_review_id","reviewer_name","reviewer_photo_url","star_rating","comment_text","review_created_at","review_updated_at","reply_text","reply_sent_at","reply_source","matched_client_id","match_confidence","entry_source","synced_at","created_at") VALUES('381f38af-1e41-4fb2-b3a0-602c54a0c2bd','AbFvOqls2evwzxEjWX7xj_9r5mmnvvXujeUPpMpSE3Fxqs-20MnjRJP_DRA3_pK5SuoJ6eow7rDZTA','Connie Schenk','https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocI7qi-iRlNAa92UWtdHR-XN0Beb3QgtxJ-XEdX8J-CDdHum-w=s120-c-rp-mo-br100',5,'Tony with Columbus Home Solutions & his crew did an amazing deck remodel for me. I absolutely love my new deck & roof! Tony is great with helping design & implement changes as you go. Love working with Tony & knowing I’ve found an individual that I can count on to follow-through.','2025-10-04T23:28:07.365443Z','2025-10-05T00:05:38.363819Z','Thank you so much for your kind words! Our team is thrilled you love your new deck and roof. We appreciate your trust!','2025-10-06T20:04:09.613288Z','external','Z2lkOi8vSm9iYmVyL0NsaWVudC8xMDg5NzI1MDc=','suggested','sync','2026-08-23 21:30:29','2026-07-20 02:06:46');
